=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play updates/by-hardn-alpine ---------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Auto Updates screen proposed for slice$
# 7, drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (updates.Auto's Read: the check, aptconf, dpkg, systemctl,$
# alpine.ReadUpdates and OtherJobs, hardn's record), each change$
# the real control's (updates.Auto, on and off) on the real$
# plan/apply engine. Nothing on this machine changes: every$
# command and file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: updates/by-hardn-alpine$
# web-01.example.net runs Alpine 3.23 (OpenRC). alpine323 after$
# hardn's Enable: apk-cron, crond at boot and running, the$
# record. Disable stops crond, takes it out of the runlevel and$
# removes apk-cron.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  apk-cron             Installed 1.0-r3$
   -  Daily Script         In place /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
   -  crond                Running starts at boot$
   -  Turned on by         hardn record of 2026-10-20$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable automatic updates$
      Undo hardn's changes$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Disable automatic updates ####################################$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
   -  Auto Updates         Off$
   -  Rollback             Reinstalls from the repositories$
$
   -  Stop crond$
      crond$
      $ rc-service crond stop$
$
   -  Stop crond at boot$
      crond$
      $ rc-update del crond default$
$
   -  Remove apk-cron$
      apk-cron$
      $ apk del apk-cron$
$
   -  Delete hardn's record$
      /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json$
$
  Turn automatic updates off? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Stop crond             Done$
  [+] Stop crond at boot     Done$
  [+] Remove apk-cron        Done$
  [+] Delete hardn's record  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /var/lib/hardn/controls/updates.auto.json kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [ ] Auto Updates         Not Configured no apk-cron$
$
# Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] apk-cron             Not installed$
  [ ] crond                Stopped not at boot$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Daily, by apk-cron$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: updates/by-hardn-alpine$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Before the first change$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ apk del --simulate apk-cron$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ rc-service crond status$
      $ apk del --simulate apk-cron$
$
   -  Applied: Stop crond$
      $ rc-service crond stop$
$
   -  Applied: Stop crond at boot$
      /etc/runlevels/default/crond$
      $ rc-update del crond default$
$
   -  Applied: Remove apk-cron$
      /etc/periodic/daily/apk$
      $ apk del apk-cron$
$

